{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2{v}^{2})^{2}+(2v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{4}+4{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{v}^{2}}=v$ since $v\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the substitution \n\n$$\nw={v}^{2}+1\\,⇒\\,\\text{d}w=2v\\,\\text{d}v,\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{w}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{w}^{3}}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}-\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69f07d26e2cc0b52fff11ef6c390a5b093fc20efdaba7e1247f508a6f35a5be3"} {"question" "q-109712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9},\n$$\n\nof radius $3.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\pi \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69f07d26e2cc0b52fff11ef6c390a5b093fc20efdaba7e1247f508a6f35a5be3"} {"question" "q-109779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "9\\pi \\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "9\\pi \\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9\\pi \\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,3{u}^{2},\\,u-v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6u & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}6u & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6u \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6u)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(-6u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{u}^{2}+4+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72{u}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4(18{u}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69f07d26e2cc0b52fff11ef6c390a5b093fc20efdaba7e1247f508a6f35a5be3"} {"question" "q-109947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "2u\\sqrt{9{u}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}"] ["math" "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-109947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u{sin}^{2}⁡v-2u{cos}^{2}⁡v,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2u)^{2}+(2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+(4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡v+16{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}(1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}=u$ since $u\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69f07d26e2cc0b52fff11ef6c390a5b093fc20efdaba7e1247f508a6f35a5be3"} {"question" "q-110019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}"] ["math" "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{1+2{u}^{2}}"] ["math" "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡v}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,u+2v,\\,2u-v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,-1,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-5,\\,-1,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1},\n$$\n\nof radius $1.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{35}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi \\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69f07d26e2cc0b52fff11ef6c390a5b093fc20efdaba7e1247f508a6f35a5be3"} {"question" "q-110551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi \\sqrt{11}"] ["math" "6\\pi \\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{15}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{17}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{35}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"} {"question" "q-110551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi \\sqrt{35}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070626/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1d9ae5b23390e7bcca3d274741f83ecc072e0733f546b3514d39d35408739b7"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2510 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
